  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A solar-powered agro-processing facility in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One of the core activities of aQysta B.V. is to support small farmers with crop selection, seeds, irrigation, training, financing and gaining market access. This service package is called the GROWN farm incubator. aQysta offers these free services, but operates on a profit-sharing model, where farmers and the company both receive income from the sale of the crops. Crucial in this model is access to reliable market partners and the price at which the agricultural goods can be sold, because this determines both aQysta&apos;s gross margin and the farmers&apos; income.aQysta is currently working with hundreds of smallholder farmers in Malawi.aQysta now aims to add more value to local harvested produce, by setting up a processing facility in Malawi that processes fresh agricultural products into dried products. To ensure stable income and to set up a sustainable business model, aQysta not only wants to sell the dried products on the local market, but also export and sell them to customers and market players outside Malawi.The aim of aQysta is therefore to establish an export value chain to customers in Europe, who are willing to sign a multi-year contract for the supply of dried products from Malawi.</narrative>
  </description>
